yers to talk and we can  debate whether or not that was the right  decision by the league but it's the  decision they made and I understand why  they made it so for Jim crane to say  well the commissioner  that he decided not to punish player  it's not quite as simple as that I think  it's a fair question and Jim crane has  kept saying well what the Commissioner  said and I agree with them do you think  that Altuve and Reddick were wearing a  wire or buzzers look I have no evidence  to believe that is true we've all seen  that it was now a Tuesday video over  2019 it's really weird but so far that's  just been the realm of conspiracy  theories and I have no reason to think  otherwise I will say though there's been  a lot of weird things in this story that  a month ago or two weeks ago I would  have said it's crazy that turned out to  be true so maybe we'll find out  different but at this moment I really  had no reason to believe that's true but  it is a good conspiracy theory though I  was wondering if this owner let's say  his players were guilty of using  steroids would he have blamed the needle  what do you blamed a doctor the training  set he wouldn't he wouldn't blame the  players he would have said well they  were led down the wrong path or  something yeah he that you might be  right and the other thing he did a lot  today was we put all the blame on Jeff  Blue now AJ handy said well I fired  those guys they were the leaders they  were responsible but what he didn't say  those guys have bosses too and their  boss was you Jim McLean the owner of the  organization he made it very clear that  he does not think that he deserves any  sort of culpability for this at all it's  the people who just worked directly  underneath him if I said you got one  question you can ask to anybody involved  in this who would it be and what would  you ask oh goodness  Jose all to me were you actually wearing  a buzzer no I don't think I'll ever  answer it truthfully but if we could  